{
  "title": "Hypophosphatasia",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9083/hypophosphatasia",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 29 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Hypophosphatasia is a metabolic bone disease caused by a mutation in the isoenzyme of alkaline phosphatase that leads to low levels of alkaline phosphate and generalized impairment of bone mineralization. Patients present with clinical manifestations similar to rickets with bow legs, short stature, abnormal teeth, and increased susceptibility to fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with the presence of phosphoethanolamine in the urine.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment modalities include enzyme replacement therapy, anti-inflammatories, and multidisciplinary care",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "severe forms (perinatal/infantile) estimated to be 1 in 100,000 to 1 in 300,000",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "milder forms (adult) estimated to be 1 in 500 to 1 in 3,000",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "significant diagnostic delay is common in both adults and children",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "low levels of alkaline phosphate result in decreased synthesis of inorganic phosphate necessary for bone matrix formation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extracellular accumulation of inorganic pyrophosphate (PPi), pyridoxal 5'-phosphate (PLP), and phosphoethanolamine (PEA)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "excess PPi inhibits hydroxyapatite crystal formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "osteoid that forms in the hypertrophic zone of the growth plate fails to mineralize",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "the zone of provisional calcification never forms and growth is inhibited",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inheritance pattern",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**severe forms (perinatal/infantile): autosomal recessive**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "mild/adult forms: often autosomal dominant",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**caused by a loss-of-function mutation in the tissue-nonspecific isoenzyme of alkaline phosphatase (TNSALP)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "orthopaedic manifestations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may resemble rickets",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "short stature",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "non-orthopaedic manifestations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "abnormal tooth formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "loss of teeth due to bone loss and dental caries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "respiratory compromise and lung hypoplasia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "hypercalcemia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "muscle weakness and fatigue",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
